s well as loans secured by savings accounts and personal credit lines. In addition, the company originates, administers, and services commercial insurance premium loans; equipment finance loans; and small business administration loans. Further, it operates full-service domestic banking offices, and mortgage and loan production offices. Ameris Bancorp was founded in 1971 and is headquartered in Atlanta, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. H. Palmer Proctor Jr. | Vice Chairman & CEO | Age 57 | Compensation: $3.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $461K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 15%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $141K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Ameris Bancorp is a mid-cap financial services business with a $5.6B market cap on $1.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +17% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $370M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 31 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.95\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 1.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 5.4% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.7\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.5% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 15% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Shares offer a 29% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","12 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Understanding Momentum Shifts in (ABCB)","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/38/Understanding_Momentum_Shifts_in_ABCB_110926053202_1794263522.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794263522.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Critical 